From: Sam Day <me@samcday.com>
Subject: [PATCH] process: store reciprocal correction gains in AsShotNeutral

The preview multiplies raw R/B channels by red/blue correction gains.
AsShotNeutral describes the raw response to a neutral subject, which is the
reciprocal of those gains. DNG decoders divide by this tag; writing gains
directly applies the opposite white balance to the saved JPEG.

The preview gains are initialized to 1 and clamped to 0.01..4 by software WB.

--- a/src/process_pipeline.c
+++ b/src/process_pipeline.c
@@ -1123,7 +1123,8 @@
         }
         libdng_set_orientation(&dng, orientation);
         libdng_set_software(&dng, "Megapixels");
-        libdng_set_neutral(&dng, state_proc.red, 1.0f, state_proc.blue);
+        libdng_set_neutral(&dng, 1.0f / state_proc.red, 1.0f,
+                           1.0f / state_proc.blue);
         libdng_set_analog_balance(&dng,
                                   state_proc.balance[0],
                                   state_proc.balance[1],
